{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F1PsjkvxbxuVv1G69JvFoW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2026\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Robot Learning Foundation\",\"url\":\"https://www.robot-learning.org/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers\",\"url\":\"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form were not directly available. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Information\n\nCoRL aims to have at least two reviewers per paper. All submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer.\n\n## Related Reviewer Guidelines\n\nWhile specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines weren't found, I did locate reviewer guidelines from previous CoRL conferences that may be helpful for context. Review criteria include assessing relevance—whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, is evaluated in simulation or on real robots, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested.\n\n## Accessing the Review Form\n\nFor the actual CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, you can access them through:\n- The official CoRL 2026 website at www.corl.org\n- The OpenReview platform at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference\n\nThese resources would have the most up-to-date information on the specific review form and detailed guidelines for CoRL 2026 reviewers.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b215f82-0f5c-4b30-b56b-cf1e505ff256","uuid":"2b2e6669-c37a-4c20-9e34-ea73e7e1affb","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:10:32.937Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01PAsBBMtvaEspZ1fcC6wVn4","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2026%2FConference"},{"title":"CoRL 2026 - Call for Papers","url":"https://www.corl.org/contributions/call-for-papers"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2026","url":"https://www.corl.org/"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"Robot Learning Foundation","url":"https://www.robot-learning.org/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers","url":"https://corl2022.org/instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"CoRL 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2025%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL 2026, though specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form were not directly available. Here's what I found:\n\n## CoRL 2026 Information\n\nCoRL aims to have at least two reviewers per paper. All submissions must include at least one author who agrees to serve as a CoRL reviewer.\n\n## Related Reviewer Guidelines\n\nWhile specific CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines weren't found, I did locate reviewer guidelines from previous CoRL conferences that may be helpful for context. Review criteria include assessing relevance—whether the paper addresses a problem in robot learning, applies or improves a learning-based method, is evaluated in simulation or on real robots, and whether the CoRL audience would be interested.\n\n## Accessing the Review Form\n\nFor the actual CoRL 2026 reviewer guidelines and review form, you can access them through:\n- The official CoRL 2026 website at www.corl.org\n- The OpenReview platform at https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org/CoRL/2026/Conference\n\nThese resources would have the most up-to-date information on the specific review form and detailed guidelines for CoRL 2026 reviewers."],"durationSeconds":5.6705084690000005}}
