{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qars696qV7nfQD78ea9fq7","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews reviewer scoring criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056528/\"},{\"title\":\"Best Reviewers Award for 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11955497/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12055280/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2024%2FConference\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the CoRL 2024 Instructions for Reviews. Here's the key information about reviewer scoring criteria:\n\n## Evaluation Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical. Results will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nReviewers need to have expertise in robotics, robot learning, machine learning and complementary fields, as demonstrated by a record of previous publications in the area. Reviewers ideally have a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences and journals (e.g. CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, IJRR, TRO, RAL) and core machine learning venues (e.g. NeurIPS, ICML, AIStats, JMLR, PAMI).\n\n## Review Process\n\nAuthors of regular paper submissions will have an opportunity to submit a response to reviewers and update the papers during the rebuttal period. Reviews and rebuttals of accepted papers will be made publicly available.\n\nThe full instructions page is available at: https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b215f82-0f5c-4b30-b56b-cf1e505ff256","uuid":"0511e563-5587-45a1-b7f8-e456a6bb3bec","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:10:45.183Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews reviewer scoring criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01VD6mZdX64TwELaCdtTk9CB","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056528/"},{"title":"Best Reviewers Award for 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11955497/"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12055280/"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=robot-learning.org%2FCoRL%2F2024%2FConference"}]},"Based on the search results, I found the CoRL 2024 Instructions for Reviews. Here's the key information about reviewer scoring criteria:\n\n## Evaluation Criteria\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical. Results will be judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\n## Reviewer Requirements\n\nReviewers need to have expertise in robotics, robot learning, machine learning and complementary fields, as demonstrated by a record of previous publications in the area. Reviewers ideally have a minimum of 3 first author publications in major robotics conferences and journals (e.g. CoRL, RSS, ICRA, IROS, IJRR, TRO, RAL) and core machine learning venues (e.g. NeurIPS, ICML, AIStats, JMLR, PAMI).\n\n## Review Process\n\nAuthors of regular paper submissions will have an opportunity to submit a response to reviewers and update the papers during the rebuttal period. Reviews and rebuttals of accepted papers will be made publicly available.\n\nThe full instructions page is available at: https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"],"durationSeconds":6.387992505999999}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017NxS8zgDE6oxN3m4ZFrktN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines scoring scale rating criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2023 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"Grant Peer Review: Improving Inter-Rater Reliability with Training\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4468126/\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965321/\"},{\"title\":\"Best Reviewers Award for 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10957073/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines page. Here's what the guidelines emphasize:\n\n## Reviewing Approach\n\nThe guidelines emphasize being constructive and concrete; courteous and respectful, starting with positive aspects and suggesting improvements. CoRL papers are required to include a limitations section, and reviewers should treat honestly reported limitations kindly and with high appreciation. \n\nHowever, obvious shortcomings or flaws not reported by the authors should be pointed out extensively and be strongly reflected in scores.\n\n## Review Standards\n\nThe guidelines provide guidance on avoiding common reviewer mistakes and emphasize that reviews should be as informative and substantiated as possible, requiring evidence when making claims about novelty or alternative approaches.\n\nUnfortunately, the search results do not contain specific details about the scoring scale (such as numerical ratings like 1-5 or 1-10) or detailed rating criteria categories for CoRL 2023. The results show that such information exists on the CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines page, but the specific scoring scale and detailed criteria were not included in the retrieved content.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b215f82-0f5c-4b30-b56b-cf1e505ff256","uuid":"23eb9096-0994-45fc-87c0-1cbd0b07d9bd","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:10:46.087Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines scoring scale rating criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014U6bDXcoTXreKBYCc8wJTp","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Statistics - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/corl-statistics/corl-2023-statistics/"},{"title":"ICLR 2023 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"Grant Peer Review: Improving Inter-Rater Reliability with Training","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4468126/"},{"title":"CoRL 2023 Accepted Paper List - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/paper-list/corl-paper-list/corl-2023-paper-list/"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2023","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10965321/"},{"title":"Best Reviewers Award for 2023","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10957073/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found the CoRL 2023 reviewer guidelines page. Here's what the guidelines emphasize:\n\n## Reviewing Approach\n\nThe guidelines emphasize being constructive and concrete; courteous an