{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018pN8Nwnqr8umvcuo4bmqHW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL OpenReview review form \"overall score\" \"confidence\" scale 1-10\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Default Review Form | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/reference/default-forms/default-review-form\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Why are the \\\"rating\\\" and \\\"confidence\\\" fields in my PC Console wrong? | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://docs.openreview.net/getting-started/frequently-asked-questions/why-are-the-rating-and-confidence-fields-in-my-pc-console-wrong\"},{\"title\":\"Simple and Efficient Confidence Score for Grading Whole Slide Images | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=DA1hOTvcMWa\"},{\"title\":\"What Have We Learned from OpenReview?\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.05885\"},{\"title\":\"Paper Ranking Methodology\",\"url\":\"https://openreview-copilot.eamag.me/ranking\"},{\"title\":\"What Drives Paper Acceptance? A Process-Centric Analysis of Modern Peer Review\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701\"},{\"title\":\"An Open Review of OpenReview: A Critical Analysis of the Machine   Learning Conference Review Process\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2010.05137\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about OpenReview review forms:\n\nThe default OpenReview review form includes a \"rating\" field with a scale from 1-10, where 10 represents \"Top 5% of accepted papers, seminal paper\" and 1 represents \"Trivial or wrong,\" along with a \"confidence\" field.\n\nThe confidence field uses a scale that includes a value of 5, described as \"The reviewer is absolutely certain that the evaluation is correct\".\n\nHowever, the search results provided general OpenReview documentation and academic papers analyzing review processes, but do not contain s