{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YX8qHGwvtSmqzqns5Ad27N","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL review form \"soundness\" \"significance\" \"novelty\" \"clarity\" rating scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://virtual.aistats.org/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2020/PaperInformation/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Novelty and Significance Technical Soundness and Content Clarity\",\"url\":\"https://www.mit.edu/~edchen93/01_asset/01_doc/2025_2-Fall_6.7960-Deep%20Learning_Final%20Project%20Grading%20Rubric.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2023 Reviewer Tutorial\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerTutorial\"},{\"title\":\"2025 Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Peer review analyze: A novel benchmark resource for computational analysis of peer reviews - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8794172/\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CoRL (Conference on Robot Learning) review guidelines:\n\nCoRL's review form asks for an evaluation of the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of work. Specifically:\n\n- **Originality**: CoRL reviewers evaluate whether the problems or methods are new, if the work is a novel combination of well-known techniques, how this work differs from previous contributions, and whether related work is adequately cited.\n\n- **Quality**: Reviewers assess whether the submission is technically sound, if claims are well supported by theoretical analysis or experimental results, if methods are appropriate, if it's complete work or work in progress, and whether authors honestly evaluate both strengths and weaknesses.\n\n- **Clarity**: Reviewers determine if the submission is clearly written, well organized, and adequately informs the reader.\n\nFor more recent CoRL reviews, submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of results (theoretical or empirical), judged on how objectively they've been established and their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as relevance to robotic learning.\n\nHowever, the search results did not reveal the specific numerical rating scale used for soundness, significance, novelty, and clarity in CoRL's review form.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3b215f82-0f5c-4b30-b56b-cf1e505ff256","uuid":"9c8b6f3b-4949-463a-b317-b6bd70decd77","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:11:06.859Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL review form \"soundness\" \"significance\" \"novelty\" \"clarity\" rating scale","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Ezc3gGeCRCVA5ZCkVzEQHj","content":[{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://virtual.aistats.org/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2020/PaperInformation/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Novelty and Significance Technical Soundness and Content Clarity","url":"https://www.mit.edu/~edchen93/01_asset/01_doc/2025_2-Fall_6.7960-Deep%20Learning_Final%20Project%20Grading%20Rubric.pdf"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"ICML 2023 Reviewer Tutorial","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2023/ReviewerTutorial"},{"title":"2025 Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/ReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"Peer review analyze: A novel benchmark resource for computational analysis of peer reviews - PMC","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8794172/"},{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about CoRL (Conference on Robot Learning) review guidelines:\n\nCoRL's review form asks for an evaluation of the originality, quality, clarity, significance, relevance and limitations of work. Specifically:\n\n- **Originality**: CoRL reviewers evaluate whether the problems or methods are new, if the work is a novel combination of well-known techniques, how this work differs from previous contributions, and whether related work is adequately cited.\n\n- **Quality**: Reviewers assess whether the submission is technically sound, if claims are well supported by theoretical analysis or experimental results, if methods are appropriate, if it's complete work or work in progress, and whether authors honestly evaluate both strengths and weaknesses.\n\n- **Clarity**: Reviewers determine if the submission is clearly written, well organized, and adequately informs the reader.\n\nFor more recent CoRL reviews, submissions are evaluated based on the significance and novelty of results (theoretical or empirical), judged on how objectively they've been established and their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as relevance to robotic learning.\n\nHowever, the search results did not reveal the specific numerical rating scale used for soundness, significance, novelty, and clarity in CoRL's review form."],"durationSeconds":6.785164018999996}}
