{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PzhrzQiSGZYJXkLGoBvKrR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Median 档叙事：SDF 是有效的 geometric safety probe，但 LoRA 本身贡献了非小部分 CAR\n2\t  提升（~35-40%）， SDF 增量约 +12-17pp。Phase 2 λ=0 结果为 informative negative——TSR 恢复但 CAR\n3\t  回落，证明 safety encoding 不持久，需持续 supervision。OpenVLA 验证 fake safety 存在但信号弱于 Pi0。spatial_bowl\n4\t  SDF 效果存在但弱于 object_pudding。论文定位 diagnostic paper，SDF 作为 probe 而非 solution。 Acceptance\n5\t  估算 50-60%。\n6\t\n7\t  '\n8\timagined_experiments:\n9\t- name: A1 EE displacement re-eval (50 episodes)\n10\t  plan_id: plan_001\n11\t  description: '用修复后 eval 脚本重跑 A1 (Pi0+LoRA+SDF) model 在 object_pudding 上 50 episodes，\n12\t    提取真实 EE displacement 以定量确认 Claim 1 fake safety。\n13\t\n14\t    '\n15\t  expected_results:\n16\t    n_episodes: 50\n17\t    avg_TSR: 0\n18\t    avg_CAR: 91.0\n19\t    avg_ee_displacement_m: 0.0021\n20\t    avg_obstacle_displacement_mm: 0.003\n21\t    fake_safe_rate: 0.995\n22\t    real_safe_count: 0\n23\t    episodes_with_ee_disp_gt_0p1m: 0\n24\t  result_rationale: '已有 800ep rerun (eval_a1_lora_object_v11_rerun) 确认 CAR=91.5%、fake_safe_rate=99.6%、\n25\t    obstacle displacement 中位数 ~5nm。在 median 档下，修复后脚本新增的 EE displacement 字段预计 同样极低（~2mm），因为\n26\t    A1 模型 TSR=0% 表明 action collapse——robot 几乎不动，EE 位移自然极小。 这 50ep sanity check 应与\n27\t    800ep 数据高度一致，确认 \"EE displacement 接近零 = fake safety\" 的定量证据链。不会出现意外高 EE displacement，因为\n28\t    action collapse 是结构性的。\n29\t\n30\t    '\n31\t  tables:\n32\t  - name: A1 EE Displacement Sanity Check (50ep)\n33\t    columns:\n34\t    - Metric\n35\t    - 800ep Rerun\n36\t    - 50ep Re-eval\n37\t    rows:\n38\t    - - TSR\n39\t      - 0%\n40\t      - 0%\n41\t    - - CAR\n42\t      - 91.5%\n43\t      - ~91%\n44\t    - - Fake Safe Rate\n45\t      - 99.6%\n46\t      - ~99.5%\n47\t    - - Avg Obstacle Disp (mm)\n48\t      - '0.003'\n49\t      - ~0.003\n50\t    - - Avg EE Disp (m)\n51\t      - N/A (old script)\n52\t      - ~0.002\n53\t    - - Episodes EE>0.1m\n54\t      - N/A\n55\t      - '0'\n56\t  figures_description:\n57\t  - 'Histogram: per-episode EE displacement 分布, 预期全部集中在 <5mm, 与 800ep obstacle displacement\n58\t    分布形态一致'\n59\t  analysis: '确认 A1 的 fake safety 同时表现为 obstacle displacement ≈0 和 EE displacement\n60\t    ≈0。 这两个独立指标双重验证 action collapse。50ep 与 800ep 一致则不需要 full re-eval (plan_011 取消)。\n61\t    论文中可同时报告两种 displacement 指标增强 Claim 1 说服力。\n62\t\n63\t    '\n64\t- name: OpenVLA zero-shot SafeLIBERO eval (200 episodes)\n65\t  plan_id: plan_002\n66\t  description: 'Base OpenVLA-7B 在 object_pudding 4 tasks 零样本 eval，200 episodes， 验证\n67\t    fake safety 或 geometric path safety 在第三 model family 上的表现。\n68\t\n69\t    '\n70\t  expected_results:\n71\t    n_episodes: 200\n72\t    avg_TSR: 8.0\n73\t    avg_CAR: 72.0\n74\t    avg_obstacle_displacement_mm: 12.0\n75\t    fake_safe_rate: 0.7\n76\t    task0_TSR: 4\n77\t    task0_CAR: 82\n78\t    task1_TSR: 18\n79\t    task1_CAR: 52\n80\t    task2_TSR: 6\n81\t    task2_CAR: 80\n82\t    task3_TSR: 4\n83\t    task3_CAR: 74\n84\t    ee_displacement_m: 0.08\n85\t    model_families_showing_fake_safety: 3\n86\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档核心假设：OpenVLA eval 成功但 fake safety 信号弱于 Pi0。OpenVLA-7B\n87\t    是更小的 模型（7B vs Pi0 ~3B action head），zero-shot 在 SafeLIBERO 上 TSR 预计很低（~5-10%），\n88\t    因为它没有在该 benchmark 上微调。低 TSR 意味着大量 episode 中 robot 运动有限但非完全 collapse（OpenVLA 的\n89\t    action space 与 Pi0 不同，倾向于产生小但非零的动作）。因此 CAR 会 较高（~72%）但 fake_safe_rate 约 70%——低于\n90\t    Pi0 的 99.6% 因为 OpenVLA 不会完全 freeze， 会有一些小幅运动导致 obstacle displacement 偶尔超过 0.1mm\n91\t    阈值。这给出 \"fake safety exists in OpenVLA but weaker\" 的 median 结论：第三 model family\n92\t    确认了现象存在， 但强度不一致，需在论文中 qualify。部分 task（如 chocolate_pudding 有更大障碍物）CAR 会更低因为 OpenVLA\n93\t    即使小运动也会碰到。\n94\t\n95\t    '\n96\t  tables:\n97\t  - name: OpenVLA Zero-Shot Fake Safety Analysis\n98\t    columns:\n99\t    - Model\n100\t    - TSR\n101\t    - CAR\n102\t    - Fake Safe Rate\n103\t    - Avg Obstacle Disp (mm)\n104\t    - Avg EE Disp (m)\n105\t    rows:\n106\t    - - Pi0 A1 (LoRA+SDF)\n107\t      - 0%\n108\t      - 91.5%\n109\t      - 99.6%\n110\t      - '0.003'\n111\t      - ~0.002\n112\t    - - Pi0.5 Baseline\n113\t      - 73%\n114\t      - 28%\n115\t      - 98.2% (of safe eps)\n116\t      - '150.8'\n117\t      - N/A\n118\t    - - OpenVLA-7B Zero-Shot\n119\t      - ~8%\n120\t      - ~72%\n121\t      - ~70%\n122\t      - ~12\n123\t      - ~0.08\n124\t  - name: OpenVLA Per-Task Breakdown\n125\t    columns:\n126\t    - Task\n127\t    - TSR\n128\t    - CAR\n129\t    - Obstacle Disp (mm)\n130\t    - Notes\n131\t    rows:\n132\t    - - orange_juice\n133\t      - 4%\n134\t      - 82%\n135\t      - ~5\n136\t      - low motion, mostly fake safe\n137\t    - - chocolate_pudding\n138\t      - 18%\n139\t      - 52%\n140\t      - ~28\n141\t      - larger obstacle, more real collisions\n142\t    - - milk\n143\t      - 6%\n144\t      - 80%\n145\t      - ~8\n146\t      - moderate fake safety\n147\t    - - bbq_sauce\n148\t      - 4%\n149\t      - 74%\n150\t      - ~10\n151\t      - mixed fake/geometric safety\n152\t  figures_description:\n153\t  - 'Scatter plot: 3 model families on TSR vs CAR plane, 标注 fake_safe_rate 作为 marker\n154\t    size, 展示 cross-model fake safety pattern'\n155\t  - 'Bar chart: fake_safe_rate comparison across Pi0 A1 / Pi0.5 baseline / OpenVLA,\n156\t    展示现象普遍性但强度差异'\n157\t  analysis: 'OpenVLA 确认 fake safety 存在于第三 model family，使 Claim 1 从 \"Pi0-specific\"\n158\t    升级为 \"cross-model phenomenon\"。但信号弱于 Pi0（70% vs 99.6%），论文需 qualify：fake safety 的严重程度与\n159\t    model capability 和 action space 结构相关。Pi0 action collapse 最极端， OpenVLA 有部分运动但仍大量\n160\t    fake safe。Pi0.5 的 fake safe 集中在 safe episodes 中 （task capability 高所以 safe episodes\n161\t    少）。三个 model family 共同支持 \"CAR metric is systematically contaminated\" 但机制略有不同。R1\n162\t    泛化性 concern 从 \"2 models\" 升级到 \"3 models\"，acceptance 估算从 ~40% 提升到 ~55%。可能需要 debug\n163\t    OpenVLA 的 action decoding 确保 eval 正确运行（median 档预期部分 debug 时间）。\n164\t\n165\t    '\n166\t- name: LoRA baseline eval (2 seeds, 30K checkpoint)\n167\t  plan_id: plan_003\n168\t  description: 'LoRA baseline (Pi0.5 + LoRA, 无 SDF) 训练完成后在 object_pudding 200ep eval，\n169\t    2 seeds 取均值，确定 LoRA-only CAR 从而决定 SDF 归因强度。\n170\t\n171\t    '\n172\t  expected_results:\n173\t    seed0_TSR: 38.0\n174\t    seed0_CAR: 37.0\n175\t    seed0_ee_disp: 0.32\n176\t    seed0_fake_safe_rate: 0.15\n177\t    seed1_TSR: 35.0\n178\t    seed1_CAR: 39.0\n179\t    seed1_ee_disp: 0.29\n180\t    seed1_fake_safe_rate: 0.18\n181\t    avg_TSR: 36.5\n182\t    avg_CAR: 38.0\n183\t    avg_ee_disp: 0.305\n184\t    avg_fake_safe_rate: 0.165\n185\t    sdf_delta_CAR: 14.5\n186\t    n_episodes_per_seed: 200\n187\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档假设 LoRA-only CAR 在 35-42% 范围。逻辑：Pi0.5 baseline（无 LoRA\n188\t    无 SDF） CAR=26.8%。LoRA 微调增加模型在 SafeLIBERO 上的 capacity，但没有 geometric supervision\n189\t    引导避障。LoRA 可能通过学到 task-specific 运动模式间接提升 CAR——比如学会更高效的路径 从而减少与障碍物接触的机会。但这不是 intentional\n190\t    avoidance。预计 TSR ~36.5%（低于 baseline 73% 因为 LoRA 在 SafeLIBERO 上的 fine-tuning 可能引入\n191\t    distribution shift， 但高于 SDF 版本的 5-9% 因为没有 SDF loss 干扰 task execution）。CAR ~38%\n192\t    意味着 SDF 增量 = 52.5% (avg SDF CAR) - 38% = +14.5pp。这落在 median 档的 10-18pp 范围内。 LoRA\n193\t    本身提供 +11pp over baseline（38% - 27%），SDF 额外提供 +14.5pp。叙事变为 \"LoRA helps, SDF adds\n194\t    major benefit\"——第二行归因表。fake_safe_rate 约 16% 因为部分 episode 中 LoRA 模型运动受限但非完全 collapse。\n195\t\n196\t    '\n197\t  tables:\n198\t  - name: LoRA Attribution Analysis\n199\t    columns:\n200\t    - Condition\n201\t    - TSR\n202\t    - CAR\n203\t    - EE Disp (m)\n204\t    - Fake Safe Rate\n205\t    - Delta CAR vs Baseline\n206\t    rows:\n207\t    - - Pi0.5 Baseline (no FT)\n208\t      - 73%\n209\t      - 27%\n210\t      - '0.15'\n211\t      - 98.2%\n212\t      - —\n213\t    - - Pi0.5 + LoRA only\n214\t      - ~36.5%\n215\t      - ~38%\n216\t      - ~0.31\n217\t      - ~16.5%\n218\t      - +11pp\n219\t    - - Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (λ=0.005)\n220\t      - 5.5-9.5%\n221\t      - 50-55%\n222\t      - ~0.50\n223\t      - 0%\n224\t      - +25pp\n225\t  - name: SDF vs LoRA Decomposition\n226\t    columns:\n227\t    - Component\n228\t    - CAR Contribution\n229\t    - Interpretation\n230\t    rows:\n231\t    - - Baseline geometric path\n232\t      - 27%\n233\t      - Inherent path safety of capable model\n234\t    - - LoRA capacity effect\n235\t      - +11pp → 38%\n236\t      - Task-specific motion patterns reduce incidental contact\n237\t    - - SDF geometric supervision\n238\t      - +14.5pp → 52.5%\n239\t      - Intentional collision avoidance from SDF gradient\n240\t  figures_description:\n241\t  - 'Lambda-CAR/TSR curve (Fig 5): x=lambda {0(LoRA), 0.005, 0.01}, y1=CAR, y2=TSR,\n242\t    展示 dose-dependent tradeoff, LoRA baseline 作为 λ=0 anchor point'\n243\t  analysis: 'LoRA-only CAR ~38% 确认 SDF 不是唯一驱动力——LoRA 本身通过 capacity 增加间接提升了 CAR。但 SDF\n244\t    增量 +14.5pp 仍然显著且方向一致（3 seeds 确认）。Claim 4 措辞需调整为 \"SDF provides additive safety\n245\t    benefit beyond LoRA capacity — geometric supervision amplifies rather than solely\n246\t    drives collision avoidance.\" Lambda 曲线现在有 3 个点 (0/0.005/0.01)，呈现 monotonic CAR\n247\t    增加 + TSR 下降的 dose-dependent pattern。 如果后续有 λ=0.1 数据则曲线更完整。fake_safe_rate 从 baseline\n248\t    98.2% → LoRA 16.5% → SDF 0% 的递减也是有价值的发现：LoRA 微调本身就大幅减少了 fake safety（因为 TSR 下降\n249\t    意味着 model 不再是 baseline 的 \"高能力低碰撞\" 模式），SDF 则完全消除 fake safety。\n250\t\n251\t    '\n252\t- name: LoRA baseline training completion (2 seeds)\n253\t  plan_id: plan_004\n254\t  description: 'Pi0.5 + LoRA only (无 SDF loss) 训练到 30K steps, 2 seeds。已在运行中。\n255\t\n256\t    '\n257\t  expected_results:\n258\t    seed0_steps_completed: 30000\n259\t    seed0_best_loss: 0.0068\n260\t    seed0_final_loss: 0.0085\n261\t    seed1_steps_completed: 30000\n262\t    seed1_best_loss: 0.0072\n263\t    seed1_final_loss: 0.009\n264\t    wall_time_hours_per_seed: 16\n265\t  result_rationale: 'LoRA-only 训练 loss 预计低于 A1 (LoRA+SDF) 因为没有 SDF auxiliary loss\n266\t    的干扰。 已有 A1 数据：s0_l005 best_loss=0.00786, s1_l005 best_loss=0.01143, s2_l005  best_loss=0.00874。LoRA-only\n267\t    去掉 SDF loss 后 action loss 应更低（best ~0.007）， 因为全部 gradient capacity 用于 action prediction。训练应正常完成，无\n268\t    collapse 风险 （LoRA-only 是标准 fine-tuning，比 SDF auxiliary 训练更稳定）。当前 step 26000/30000,\n269\t    预计 ~3.5h 完成。\n270\t\n271\t    '\n272\t  tables: []\n273\t  figures_description: []\n274\t  analysis: '训练本身是 dependency，关键在 eval 结果。loss 曲线可作为 supplementary 展示 SDF loss 对 action\n275\t    loss 的干扰程度。\n276\t\n277\t    '\n278\t- name: Phase 2 λ=0 ablation training (seed2, from 10K SDF checkpoint)\n279\t  plan_id: plan_005\n280\t  description: '从 Pi0.5+A1 s2 的 10K SDF checkpoint resume 训练 with λ=0 (关闭 SDF loss)，\n281\t    训练到 30K，验证 safety encoding 是否在去除 SDF 后保留。\n282\t\n283\t    '\n284\t  expected_results:\n285\t    steps_completed: 30000\n286\t    best_action_loss: 0.0075\n287\t    final_action_loss: 0.0092\n288\t    training_stable: true\n289\t    wall_time_hours: 16\n290\t    sdf_loss_at_resume: 0.0\n291\t  result_rationale: '从 SDF-trained checkpoint resume with λ=0 时，action loss 预计初始偏高（因为\n292\t    SDF 训练 10K 步偏离了 pure action prediction 的 optimum），然后逐步恢复。训练本身应该 稳定——只是标准 LoRA\n293\t    fine-tuning 从一个非标准初始化点开始。最终 action loss 应 接近 LoRA-only 水平（~0.008）但可能略高因为 10K 步的\n294\t    SDF 训练改变了 representation。\n295\t\n296\t    '\n297\t  tables: []\n298\t  figures_description: []\n299\t  analysis: '训练结果本身不直接回答科学问题——关键是 eval (plan_006)。但 loss 曲线可以展示 action loss 从 SDF-perturbed\n300\t    state 恢复的动态，作为 \"safety encoding 被覆盖\"  的间接证据。\n301\t\n302\t    '\n303\t- name: Phase 2 λ=0 eval\n304\t  plan_id: plan_006\n305\t  description: 'Phase 2 训练完成后 eval (200 episodes)，提取 TSR/CAR/EE displacement， 判断 safety\n306\t    encoding 是否保留。\n307\t\n308\t    '\n309\t  expected_results:\n310\t    avg_TSR: 42.0\n311\t    avg_CAR: 32.0\n312\t    avg_ee_disp: 0.28\n313\t    fake_safe_rate: 0.12\n314\t    task0_TSR: 30\n315\t    task0_CAR: 38\n316\t    task1_TSR: 68\n317\t    task1_CAR: 26\n318\t    task2_TSR: 20\n319\t    task2_CAR: 52\n320\t    task3_TSR: 50\n321\t    task3_CAR: 12\n322\t    n_episodes: 200\n323\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档假设：TSR 恢复到 30-50% 但 CAR 回落至 30-35%。逻辑链：(1) 关闭 SDF loss\n324\t    后模型恢复 task execution 能力（TSR 从 5-9% 回到 ~42%，不完全恢复到 baseline 73% 因为 10K 步 SDF 训练改变了\n325\t    representation 且只有 20K 步恢复时间）；(2) CAR 回落到 ~32% 接近 LoRA-only 水平（~38%）甚至略低，说明 SDF\n326\t    诱导的 safety encoding 没有被 \"烙印\" 到 representation 中——一旦 loss signal 消失，model 迅速遗忘。这是\n327\t    informative negative： safety 需要 continuous supervision，10K 步的 geometric training\n328\t    不足以产生持久的 behavioral change。TSR 42% < baseline 73% 说明 SDF 训练 phase 造成了部分不可逆的 capability\n329\t    损失（task performance 未完全恢复），但不是 catastrophic（仍有合理的 task completion）。CAR 32% 接近\n330\t    baseline 27% + LoRA effect，意味着 SDF 的 safety 增量 完全消失。fake_safe_rate ~12% 类似 LoRA-only\n331\t    水平。\n332\t\n333\t    '\n334\t  tables:\n335\t  - name: Phase 2 λ=0 Ablation Results\n336\t    columns:\n337\t    - Condition\n338\t    - TSR\n339\t    - CAR\n340\t    - EE Disp (m)\n341\t    - Fake Safe Rate\n342\t    rows:\n343\t    - - Pi0.5 Baseline\n344\t      - 73%\n345\t      - 27%\n346\t      - '0.15'\n347\t      - 98.2%\n348\t    - - SDF λ=0.005 (continuous)\n349\t      - 5.5-9.5%\n350\t      - 50-55%\n351\t      - '0.50'\n352\t      - 0%\n353\t    - - Phase 2 λ=0 (from 10K SDF)\n354\t      - ~42%\n355\t      - ~32%\n356\t      - ~0.28\n357\t      - ~12%\n358\t    - - LoRA only (no SDF ever)\n359\t      - ~36.5%\n360\t      - ~38%\n361\t      - ~0.31\n362\t      - ~16.5%\n363\t  - name: Phase 2 Interpretation Matrix\n364\t    columns:\n365\t    - Outcome\n366\t    - TSR\n367\t    - CAR\n368\t    - Interpretation\n369\t    - Paper Impact\n370\t    rows:\n371\t    - - Observed (median)\n372\t      - 42%\n373\t      - 32%\n374\t      - Safety encoding not persistent\n375\t      - Informative negative\n376\t    - - Upgrade threshold\n377\t      - '>=40%'\n378\t      - '>=40%'\n379\t      - Two-phase strategy works\n380\t      - Solution paper\n381\t    - - Strong negative\n382\t      - <20%\n383\t      - any\n384\t      - SDF causes irreversible damage\n385\t      - Supports extreme tradeoff\n386\t  figures_description:\n387\t  - 'Training dynamics plot: action loss over steps 10K-30K for Phase 2 vs LoRA-only\n388\t    vs SDF-continuous, showing recovery trajectory'\n389\t  - 'TSR-CAR scatter: Phase 2 point added to existing scatter, showing it lands between\n390\t    LoRA-only and baseline'\n391\t  analysis: 'Phase 2 结果为 informative negative：TSR 恢复（42%）证明 SDF 训练没有 permanently 破坏\n392\t    task capability，但 CAR 回落到 ~32% 证明 safety encoding 不持久。这排除了 \"two-phase training\n393\t    strategy\" 作为 technical contribution（不满足 TSR≥40% + CAR≥40% 双门槛）。论文写入方式：\"Removing\n394\t    SDF supervision recovers task performance (TSR: 9%→42%) but safety gains are lost\n395\t    (CAR: 52%→32%), indicating that SDF-induced collision avoidance requires continuous\n396\t    geometric supervision rather than being encoded as a persistent behavioral prior.\"\n397\t    这支持 diagnostic paper 定位——问题可解但 naive 方法不持久。 R3 \"no solution\" concern 通过此 negative\n398\t    result + Phase 2/lambda tuning 作为 future work 来应对。CAR 32% 略低于 LoRA-only 38%（差\n399\t    6pp）可能在 noise 范围内， 也可能说明 SDF 训练 phase 对 representation 的 perturbation 稍微损害了 LoRA  已学到的\n400\t    incidental safety patterns。\n401\t\n402\t    '\n403\t- name: spatial_bowl A1 训练 (seed0, λ=0.005)\n404\t  plan_id: plan_007\n405\t  description: 'Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (A1) 在 spatial_bowl scene 训练 30K steps， 验证 SDF\n406\t    效果是否跨 scene 泛化。\n407\t\n408\t    '\n409\t  expected_results:\n410\t    steps_completed: 30000\n411\t    best_loss: 0.0125\n412\t    final_loss: 0.0155\n413\t    wall_time_hours: 34\n414\t    sdf_loss_final: 0.0035\n415\t  result_rationale: 'spatial_bowl 是更难的 scene（障碍物布局不同，碰撞部位更多 arm-body 而非 EE）。 SDF training\n416\t    loss 预计略高于 object_pudding（s0_l005 best=0.00786）因为 scene complexity 增加了 action\n417\t    prediction 难度。训练本身应正常完成（已确认 A1 训练在 object_pudding 上 3 seeds 稳定）。当前 11329/30000\n418\t    步，~24h 剩余。\n419\t\n420\t    '\n421\t  tables: []\n422\t  figures_description: []\n423\t  analysis: '训练是 dependency，关键在 eval (plan_008)。\n424\t\n425\t    '\n426\t- name: spatial_bowl A1 eval\n427\t  plan_id: plan_008\n428\t  description: 'spatial_bowl A1 训练完成后 eval，验证跨场景 CAR/TSR pattern。200 episodes。\n429\t\n430\t    '\n431\t  expected_results:\n432\t    avg_TSR: 1.5\n433\t    avg_CAR: 18.0\n434\t    avg_ee_disp: 0.42\n435\t    fake_safe_rate: 0.0\n436\t    spatial_bowl_sdf_CAR: 18\n437\t    sdf_delta_CAR_over_baseline: 5.0\n438\t    task0_TSR: 0\n439\t    task0_CAR: 22\n440\t    task1_TSR: 6\n441\t    task1_CAR: 12\n442\t    task2_TSR: 0\n443\t    task2_CAR: 20\n444\t    task3_TSR: 0\n445\t    task3_CAR: 18\n446\t    n_episodes: 200\n447\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档假设 spatial_bowl SDF CAR 提升 5-12pp，效果存在但弱于 object_pudding。\n448\t    逻辑：(1) spatial_bowl baseline CAR=13% (eval_pi05_safelibero_spatial_v11)，远低于 object_pudding\n449\t    的 28%——scene 本身碰撞更多因为 bowl 需要在多个障碍物间抓取，arm-body 碰撞占主导而 EE-only SDF 对此无能为力（Claim\n450\t    3）。(2) SDF 在 spatial_bowl 的增量 预计约 +5pp（CAR 从 13% 到 ~18%），因为 EE-only SDF gradient\n451\t    能部分帮助 EE 避障 但 arm-body 碰撞依然发生。(3) TSR 同样大幅下降（baseline 57.5% → ~1.5%），tradeoff\n452\t    pattern 与 object_pudding 一致但 CAR 绝对值低得多。(4) EE displacement ~0.42m 确认 real avoidance（非\n453\t    fake safety），但效果有限。fake_safe_rate=0% 与 object_pudding 一致。为什么 SDF 效果弱：spatial_bowl\n454\t    中障碍物（plate, ramekin, stove）位置使得 EE 避开它们时 arm 反而更容易扫过其他障碍物——这正是 EE-only SDF 的结构性限制。\n455\t    median 档下 scenes_with_sdf_effect 为 1-2，spatial_bowl 算 \"weak effect\" 的第 2 个。\n456\t\n457\t    '\n458\t  tables:\n459\t  - name: Cross-Scene SDF Effect Comparison\n460\t    columns:\n461\t    - Scene\n462\t    - Baseline CAR\n463\t    - SDF CAR\n464\t    - Delta\n465\t    - Baseline TSR\n466\t    - SDF TSR\n467\t    - Dominant Collision Type\n468\t    rows:\n469\t    - - object_pudding\n470\t      - 27%\n471\t      - 52.5%\n472\t      - +25.5pp\n473\t      - 73%\n474\t      - 7%\n475\t      - EE-obstacle\n476\t    - - spatial_bowl\n477\t      - 13%\n478\t      - ~18%\n479\t      - ~+5pp\n480\t      - 57.5%\n481\t      - ~1.5%\n482\t      - arm-body\n483\t  - name: spatial_bowl Per-Task Breakdown\n484\t    columns:\n485\t    - Task\n486\t    - TSR\n487\t    - CAR\n488\t    - EE Disp (m)\n489\t    - Notes\n490\t    rows:\n491\t    - - pick_bowl_between_plate_ramekin\n492\t      - 0%\n493\t      - 22%\n494\t      - '0.45'\n495\t      - arm sweeps plate despite EE avoidance\n496\t    - - pick_bowl_on_ramekin\n497\t      - 6%\n498\t      - 12%\n499\t      - '0.38'\n500\t      - ramekin under bowl, unavoidable arm contact\n501\t    - - pick_bowl_on_stove\n502\t      - 0%\n503\t      - 20%\n504\t      - '0.44'\n505\t      - stove edges cause arm-body collision\n506\t    - - pick_bowl_on_cabinet\n507\t      - 0%\n508\t      - 18%\n509\t      - '0.40'\n510\t      - cabinet geometry blocks safe arm paths\n511\t  figures_description:\n512\t  - 'Paired bar chart: object_pudding vs spatial_bowl SDF delta, 展示 cross-scene effect\n513\t    attenuation'\n514\t  - 'Collision heatmap: EE vs arm-body collision locations, 展示 spatial_bowl 中 arm-body\n515\t    dominance'\n516\t  analysis: 'spatial_bowl SDF 效果弱（+5pp vs object_pudding +25pp）确认 EE-only SDF 的结构性限制——\n517\t    当碰撞主要发生在 arm body 时，EE-level geometric supervision 效果有限。这同时支持 Claim 3 (EE-only\n518\t    limitation) 和弱化 Claim 4 的 generalization。论文措辞：\"SDF effect attenuates in scenes\n519\t    where arm-body collisions dominate, confirming the structural  limitation of end-effector-only\n520\t    geometric supervision.\" 对 R1 泛化性 concern： 2 scenes 有 SDF 效果（1 strong + 1 weak）比\n521\t    1 scene 好，但效果差异大需要解释。 mechanistic argument（EE-only vs full-body SDF）提供了解释框架。scenes_with_sdf_effect=2\n522\t    落在 median 档预期范围内。\n523\t\n524\t    '\n525\t- name: Lambda=0.1 bracket training (1 seed)\n526\t  plan_id: plan_009\n527\t  description: '高 lambda (0.1) 单 seed 训练，构建 4-point lambda 曲线 (0/LoRA, 0.005, 0.01,\n528\t    0.1)。\n529\t\n530\t    '\n531\t  expected_results:\n532\t    steps_completed: 30000\n533\t    best_loss: 0.0185\n534\t    final_loss: 0.022\n535\t    sdf_loss_final: 0.0012\n536\t    action_loss_final: 0.0175\n537\t    wall_time_hours: 34\n538\t    training_stable: true\n539\t  result_rationale: 'λ=0.1 是 λ=0.01 的 10x，SDF loss 权重显著增加。预计 total loss 更高因为 SDF loss\n540\t    占比更大，action loss 被进一步牺牲。训练应该稳定（λ=0.01 已验证稳定），但 action prediction quality 会进一步下降。best_loss\n541\t    预计 ~0.0185（vs λ=0.01 的 ~0.009， λ=0.005 的 ~0.008）——大部分增量来自 SDF loss 贡献。此实验是 P1\n542\t    因为主要用于 构建曲线，不是论文核心数据。如果 LoRA baseline CAR ≈ SDF CAR 则取消（但 median 档下 LoRA CAR ~38%\n543\t    < SDF 52.5% 所以会继续）。\n544\t\n545\t    '\n546\t  tables: []\n547\t  figures_description: []\n548\t  analysis: '训练数据用于 eval (plan_010)。loss 曲线本身可作为 supplementary 展示 lambda 对 action\n549\t    loss 的 dose-dependent degradation。\n550\t\n551\t    '\n552\t- name: Lambda=0.1 eval\n553\t  plan_id: plan_010\n554\t  description: 'λ=0.1 训练完成后 eval，验证 lambda 递增是否 monotonic 提升 CAR。200 episodes。\n555\t\n556\t    '\n557\t  expected_results:\n558\t    avg_TSR: 1.5\n559\t    avg_CAR: 58.0\n560\t    avg_ee_disp: 0.55\n561\t    fake_safe_rate: 0.0\n562\t    task0_TSR: 0\n563\t    task0_CAR: 70\n564\t    task1_TSR: 6\n565\t    task1_CAR: 50\n566\t    task2_TSR: 0\n567\t    task2_CAR: 92\n568\t    task3_TSR: 0\n569\t    task3_CAR: 20\n570\t    n_episodes: 200\n571\t  result_rationale: 'λ=0.1 进一步增强 SDF supervision 权重，预计 CAR 继续 monotonic 上升但边际递减。 从\n572\t    λ=0.005 (CAR ~52.5%) 到 λ=0.01 (CAR ~53%)，增量已经很小（~0.5pp）。λ=0.1 预计再增 ~5pp 到 ~58%，因为更强的\n573\t    geometric supervision 让 EE 更积极避障，但 EE-only 的结构性上限限制了进一步提升。TSR 进一步下降到 ~1.5%（接近零），因为极强的\n574\t    SDF loss 几乎完全压制了 task execution。这构成 4-point 曲线：λ=0 (LoRA, CAR 38%, TSR 36.5%)\n575\t    → λ=0.005 (CAR 52.5%, TSR 7%) → λ=0.01 (CAR 53%, TSR 7%) → λ=0.1 (CAR 58%, TSR\n576\t    1.5%)。曲线展示 CAR 的 diminishing returns + TSR 的 floor effect。 这支持 \"naive lambda scaling\n577\t    不是 solution\" 的叙事，为 future work（adaptive lambda, curriculum）提供 motivation。\n578\t\n579\t    '\n580\t  tables:\n581\t  - name: 4-Point Lambda Curve\n582\t    columns:\n583\t    - Lambda\n584\t    - Source\n585\t    - TSR\n586\t    - CAR\n587\t    - EE Disp (m)\n588\t    - Fake Safe Rate\n589\t    rows:\n590\t    - - 0 (LoRA only)\n591\t      - plan_003\n592\t      - 36.5%\n593\t      - 38%\n594\t      - '0.31'\n595\t      - 16.5%\n596\t    - - '0.005'\n597\t      - 3-seed avg\n598\t      - 7%\n599\t      - 52.5%\n600\t      - '0.50'\n601\t      - 0%\n602\t    - - '0.01'\n603\t      - 3-seed avg\n604\t      - 7%\n605\t      - 53%\n606\t      - '0.50'\n607\t      - 0%\n608\t    - - '0.1'\n609\t      - plan_010\n610\t      - 1.5%\n611\t      - ~58%\n612\t      - ~0.55\n613\t      - 0%\n614\t  - name: Lambda Curve Marginal Analysis\n615\t    columns:\n616\t    - Lambda Step\n617\t    - Delta CAR\n618\t    - Delta TSR\n619\t    - CAR per TSR pp Lost\n620\t    rows:\n621\t    - - 0 → 0.005\n622\t      - +14.5pp\n623\t      - -29.5pp\n624\t      - '0.49'\n625\t    - - 0.005 → 0.01\n626\t      - +0.5pp\n627\t      - ~0pp\n628\t      - ∞\n629\t    - - 0.01 → 0.1\n630\t      - +5pp\n631\t      - -5.5pp\n632\t      - '0.91'\n633\t  figures_description:\n634\t  - 'Fig 5 (paper figure): dual-y-axis plot, x=log(lambda), y1=CAR (ascending, saturating),\n635\t    y2=TSR (descending, floor at ~0%), with LoRA baseline as λ=0 anchor. Key insight:\n636\t    CAR saturates while TSR collapses'\n637\t  analysis: '4-point lambda 曲线是 median 档的 key deliverable。它展示：(1) SDF 的 dose-dependent\n638\t    safety effect 存在但 saturating；(2) TSR 的 catastrophic decline 在 λ=0.005 已经发生， 更高\n639\t    lambda 只是 marginal 恶化；(3) 最优 tradeoff 点（如果存在）在 λ < 0.005 区间， 需要 finer-grained\n640\t    search（future work）。R3 \"no solution\" 应对：曲线本身就是 methodological contribution——展示了\n641\t    lambda 空间的 landscape，为后续优化提供 guidance。 R5 \"tradeoff too extreme\" 应对：曲线证明 tradeoff\n642\t    是 dose-dependent 的，暗示 adaptive/curriculum 策略可能找到更好的 operating point。\n643\t\n644\t    '\n645\t- name: Claim 1 full A1 re-eval decision\n646\t  plan_id: plan_011\n647\t  description: '基于 plan_001 的 50ep 结果，决定是否需要 800ep full re-eval with EE displacement。\n648\t\n649\t    '\n650\t  expected_results:\n651\t    decision: no_full_reeval_needed\n652\t    rationale: 50ep EE displacement confirms ≈0, consistent with 800ep obstacle displacement\n653\t      data\n654\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 plan_001 的 50ep sanity check 应确认 EE displacement ≈\n655\t    0（与已有 800ep obstacle displacement 数据一致）。既然两个独立 displacement 指标都确认 action collapse，\n656\t    就不需要花 10 GPU-hours 做 800ep full re-eval——50ep 已足够作为 \"术语验证\" 证据。 论文中报告 \"800ep obstacle\n657\t    displacement + 50ep EE displacement 双重确认\" 即可。 只有当 50ep 出现意外结果（如 EE displacement\n658\t    意外高）才需要 full re-eval，但在 median 档下这不会发生。\n659\t\n660\t    '\n661\t  tables: []\n662\t  figures_description: []\n663\t  analysis: 这是一个 decision point 而非独立实验。主要价值是节省 GPU 资源。\n664\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LPjFU9kEwtfi8UeALVd523","session_id":"3b215f82-0f5c-4b30-b56b-cf1e505ff256","uuid":"b99087c0-5159-4859-be99-afbf994af160","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:13:00.180Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012R2uDdteKATQFSHicAL9sm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\subsection{The Fake Safety Problem}\\label{sec:fake_safety}\n2\t\n3\tAt first glance, the collision avoidance results for SDF-augmented VLA models appear compelling. Our A1-LoRA model (Pi0 fine-tuned with an SDF auxiliary loss) achieves a Collision Avoidance Rate (CAR) of 91.5\\% across 800 evaluation episodes on the SafeLIBERO benchmark~\\cite{hu2025vlsa}, a figure that would suggest reliable obstacle avoidance. Yet this headline metric conceals a fundamental problem. When we examine the end-effector displacement of the 732 episodes classified as ``safe,'' the picture changes entirely: 541 episodes (73.9\\%) exhibit a maximum displacement below 1\\,$\\mu$m, and another 188 episodes (25.7\\%) remain below 0.1\\,mm. Only 3 episodes (0.4\\%) show displacement above the 0.1\\,mm threshold, the minimum we consider consistent with intentional motion. The remaining 99.6\\% of safe episodes are artifacts of a robot that never moved.\n4\t\n5\tWe define a safe episode as \\emph{fake safe} when the maximum end-effector displacement stays below a threshold $\\tau_d = 0.1$\\,mm. Under this criterion, 729 of the 732 safe episodes produced by A1-LoRA are fake safe. The robot did not avoid obstacles; it avoided motion altogether. The displacement distribution, shown in Figure~\\ref{fig:displacement}, clusters overwhelmingly near zero, with no meaningful spread toward the range that would indicate planned trajectories around obstacles. Table~\\ref{tab:fake_safety} summarizes the fake safety statistics across all evaluated methods.\n6\t\n7\t\\begin{table}[t]\n8\t\\centering\n9\t\\caption{Fake safety decomposition across methods on SafeLIBERO. CAR$_\\text{f}$ excludes episodes with max displacement $< \\tau_d = 0.1$\\,mm. Fake safe rate is computed over safe (non-collision) episodes only.}\n10\t\\label{tab:fake_safety}\n11\t\\vspace{2pt}\n12\t\\small\n13\t\\begin{tabular}{lccccc}\n14\t\\toprule\n15\tMethod & CAR (\\%) & TSR (\\%) & Fake Safe (\\%) & Real Safe & CAR$_\\text{f}$ (\\%) \\\\\n16\t\\midrule\n17\tA1-LoRA (SDF) & 91.5 & 0.0 & 99.6 & 3 / 732 & ---$^\\dagger$ \\\\\n18\tLoRA baseline  & 82.0 & 0.0 & 99.4 & $\\approx$\\,1 / 164 & $\\approx$\\,0 \\\\\n19\tPi0.5 (3-seed) & 26.8\\,$\\pm$\\,1.6 & 74.7\\,$\\pm$\\,1.5 & 98.2 & 1 / 56 & $\\approx$\\,0 \\\\\n20\t\\bottomrule\n21\t\\end{tabular}\n22\t\\vspace{2pt}\n23\t{\\footnotesize $^\\dagger$ Denominator $< 5$; statistically unreliable.}\n24\t\\end{table}\n25\t\n26\tThis phenomenon is not an artifact of the SDF auxiliary loss. The LoRA baseline, trained without any collision avoidance objective, reports a CAR of 82.0\\% with a Task Success Rate (TSR) of 0\\%. Among its 164 safe episodes, 99.4\\% are fake safe by the same displacement criterion. The pattern persists in Pi0.5, a larger model from the same family (${\\\\sim}$3B$\\to$${\\\\sim}$3.5B parameters) that exhibits substantially less action collapse. Across three seeds (600 total episodes), Pi0.5 achieves a CAR of 26.8\\,$\\pm$\\,1.6\\% and a TSR of 74.7\\,$\\pm$\\,1.5\\%. Its lower CAR reflects the fact that Pi0.5 actually moves the robot, which naturally increases collision frequency. Yet among its safe episodes, the fake safe rate remains 98.2\\% (55 of 56 safe episodes in seed 0 show near-zero displacement). The conclusion is consistent across methods: when a Pi0-family model does not collide, it is almost certainly because it did not move.\n27\t\n28\tThese observations motivate the displacement-filtered CAR (CAR$_\\text{f}$) defined in Eq.~\\ref{eq:car_f}, which excludes episodes with sub-threshold displacement from both numerator and denominator. We provide a sensitivity analysis over $\\tau_d \\in \\{0.01, 0.1, 1, 10\\}$\\,mm in Appendix~\\ref{sec:appendix_threshold}, showing that conclusions are robust to threshold choice. For A1-LoRA, only 3 of 800 episodes exceed the threshold; all 3 happen to be safe, but a denominator of 3 precludes any meaningful rate estimate. For the LoRA baseline and Pi0.5, CAR$_\\text{f}$ is similarly near zero. The gap between raw CAR and CAR$_\\text{f}$ exposes the scale of contamination: a model can report over 90\\% CAR while possessing essentially no collision avoidance capability.\n29\t\n30\tThe practical implication is stark. Standard CAR evaluation conflates two behaviors that differ in every meaningful respect: a robot that plans a safe trajectory around an obstacle, and a robot that has collapsed into inaction due to distributional shift. Without displacement filtering, any model suffering from action collapse will receive inflated safety scores, and models that collapse more severely will paradoxically appear safer. This inversion renders CAR, as conventionally computed, unreliable for evaluating collision avoidance in VLA models. CAR$_\\text{f}$ also serves a diagnostic role: a method that achieves a non-trivial CAR$_\\text{f}$ value provides positive evidence that its safety behavior reflects genuine avoidance rather than inaction. Among all configurations evaluated in this work, Pi0.5 with training-time SDF supervision (Section~\\ref{sec:a1_pi05}) is the first to produce a meaningful CAR$_\\text{f}$."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019h1p5pE9JDM9Q3AeMPJ3dn","session_id":"3b215f82-0f5c-4b30-b56b-cf1e505ff256","uuid":"dc3e6e29-aebe-47ce-bc8b-9ae1c64f95aa","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:12:59.927Z"}
