{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WfwH19kZFyTQwxhQqHEC9J","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515/projects/diff_collision_sdf/decisions.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"_next_id: 24\\\\ndecisions:\\\\n- id: D001\\\\n  date: 2026-05-19 16:08 UTC\\\\n  summary: 锁定 π0/openpi 为 MVP 基座模型，补充 Phase A kill gates 和可复现性协议\\\\n  rationale: 采纳 Reviewer 4 条 warning：(1) π0 flow matching 连续动作空间天然适配 SDF 梯度修正，OpenVLA\\\\n    autoregressive token 预测需额外离散→连续映射；(2) 10%-20% 成功率下降定义为 conditional pass 消除灰色地带；(3)\\\\n    Phase A 增加 3 个 kill gate（MuJoCo 版本、mesh 可访问性、梯度回传 toy test）；(4) 3 seeds × 50 episodes\\\\n    保证统计显著性。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D002\\\\n  date: 2026-05-19 16:19 UTC\\\\n  summary: 维持 D001 π0/openpi 决策，Worker 推荐 OpenVLA-OFT 被否决\\\\n  rationale: Worker 推荐 OFT 基于\\\\\\\"ODE 多步梯度传播劣势\\\\\\\"论点，但 Reviewer 修正：(1) 训练时 π0 不跑 ODE solver，单步去噪梯度回传无劣势；(2)\\\\n    推理时多步 ODE 反而是优势——每步去噪可注入 SDF gradient correction，实现迭代式轨迹优化，这是 IDEA_BRIEF 核心机制\\\\n    \\\\\\\"SDF-gradient-guided action refinement\\\\\\\" 的天然载体；(3) 2.5B vs 7B，MVP 快速迭代 π0 有 2-3x\\\\n    速度优势。OpenVLA-OFT 记录为工程 fallback。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D001\\\\n- id: D003\\\\n  date: 2026-05-19 17:42 UTC\\\\n  summary: KG-2 conditional pass，接受非 watertight 风险，要求 SDF GT 预计算时验证梯度方向 + 翻转符号约定\\\\n  rationale: 81.4% robosuite mesh 非 watertight，trimesh repair 失败。但 pysdf 在非 watertight\\\\n    mesh 上仍返回合理 SDF 值，且 MVP 只需 1-2 个场景可用。关键要求：(1) SDF GT 生成时取负翻转符号约定（pysdf 正=内部 →\\\\n    标准正=外部）(2) 对 MVP 场景的实际 mesh 验证 SDF 梯度方向指向远离障碍物 (3) 可视化确认 SDF 场质量。不阻塞 Phase B 启动。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D001\\\\n- id: D004\\\\n  date: 2026-05-19 17:54 UTC\\\\n  summary: 批准 Phase B 启动：三步走——openpi baseline 验证 pipeline → A1 SDF auxiliary → A3\\\\n    gradient-guided，4 卡并行\\\\n  rationale: Phase A Kill Gates 全部 PASS（KG-1 MuJoCo 3.8.1，KG-2 梯度方向 >98% 准确，KG-3 梯度回传稳定）。SDF\\\\n    GT 已预计算（符号已翻转），代码框架已完成。Reviewer 两个 warning 需在集成时修复：(1) EEPositionExtractor 需加\\\\n    FK 监督 loss (2) sdf_data.py 确认不二次翻转符号。先用 1 seed 跑通 baseline 验证 pipeline，再 3 组 ×\\\\n    3 seeds 并行铺开。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D001\\\\n  - D002\\\\n  - D003\\\\n- id: D005\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 14:33 UTC\\\\n  summary: 暂停 baseline_s1，MVP 只需 1 seed/method；SAVE_TOTAL_LIMIT 降至 2 防磁盘再爆\\\\n  rationale: westd-35807 autodl-tmp 再次 100% 满，baseline_s1 在 step 15999 崩溃。4 实验 × 3\\\\n    checkpoints × 11GB = 132GB checkpoint 空间不够。baseline_s1 是 seed 1 冗余实验，MVP gate\\\\n    check 只需 1 seed per method。暂停 s1 释放 ~33GB + SAVE_TOTAL_LIMIT 2 每实验再省 11GB = 总释放\\\\n    ~77GB，保住 baseline_s0 + object_pudding + A1 三个关键实验。seed 扩展留到 research 阶段。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: baseline_spatial_bowl_s1_v2\\\\n    role: 暂停\\\\n    result: step 15999 磁盘满崩溃，不恢复\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D006\\\\n  date: 2026-05-20 20:43 UTC\\\\n  summary: 停止 A1 实验，释放 GPU 启动 LoRA baseline；A3 和当前 full-FT baseline 继续\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 发现：(1) A1 的 Phase 2 LoRA 解冻从未生效（参数名无 \\\\\\\"lora\\\\\\\" 匹配），backbone 全程冻结仅\\\\n    658K 可训练参数，loss 平台期印证；(2) Baseline 实际是 3.5B 全参 fine-tune 非 LoRA；(3) A3 自建 inject_lora()\\\\n    正常工作（~50M params，loss 正常下降）。决策：停 A1×2 释放 cuda:1/3，立即启动 LoRA baseline×2（移植 A3 的\\\\n    inject_lora）；当前 full-FT baseline 跑完用于初步 eval；A3 继续。初步 MVP gate 用 A3 vs full-FT\\\\n    baseline（若 50M LoRA 胜 3.5B full-FT 更强），正式 gate 用 A3 vs LoRA baseline。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: a1_sdf_spatial_bowl_s0_v3\\\\n    role: stopped\\\\n    result: backbone frozen, LoRA unfreeze failed\\\\n  - exp_id: a1_sdf_object_pudding_s0\\\\n    role: stopped\\\\n    result: backbone frozen, LoRA unfreeze failed\\\\n  - exp_id: a3_gradient_spatial_bowl_s0\\\\n    role: continue\\\\n    result: inject_lora working correctly\\\\n  - exp_id: a3_gradient_object_pudding_s0\\\\n    role: continue\\\\n    result: inject_lora working correctly\\\\n  depends_on: []\\\\n- id: D007\\\\n  date: 2026-05-21 17:39 UTC\\\\n  summary: MVP gate 分级：1 scene PASS → conditional pass 启动 post-MVP 规划，2 scenes PASS\\\\n    → full pass\\\\n  rationale: 'A3 spatial_bowl 三次失败后从 step 6001 重启，ETA ~27h。等两个 scene 全部完成再判 MVP 会浪费\\\\n    27h。1 scene (object_pudding) 若 CAR ≥15% + TSR <10%，已足够验证核心假设（SDF gradient refinement\\\\n    有效），可 conditional pass 启动 paper_framing + experiment_plan，同时 spatial_bowl 作为后续确认。Reviewer\\\\n    warning #5 驱动。'\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: a3_gradient_object_pudding_s0\\\\n    role: primary_mvp_gate\\\\n    result: pending\\\\n  - exp_id: a3_gradient_spatial_bowl_s0\\\\n    role: secondary_confirmation\\\\n    result: running_from_step_6001\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D005\\\\n- id: D008\\\\n  date: 2026-05-22 19:41 UTC\\\\n  summary: A3 方向暂停常规 eval，优先实现 true oracle 上界实验（GT SDF + 数值梯度）确定方法天花板\\\\n  rationale: M026/M027/M028 三个 bug 导致 A3 runtime refinement 从未被正确测试。在修复前所有 eval 结果无效。true\\\\n    oracle（绕过 learned decoder，用 GT 点云 + 数值梯度）是确定方法上界的最快路径（2-4h 实现 + 1-2h 运行）。如果 true\\\\n    oracle 也失败 → A3 runtime refine 方向根本不可行；如果成功 → 修复 decoder + 对齐 train/eval 后方向活。A1（training-time\\\\n    SDF）不受影响，继续并行验证。Spatial scope 收窄到 object tasks（spatial arm-body 碰撞确认 EE-only SDF\\\\n    无效）。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: oracle_a3_m024fix_object_v11\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: fake safety (137/160 frozen, 23/23 collision when moving)\\\\n  - exp_id: oracle_a3_force_refine_object_v11\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: 'invalid (M027: oracle dead code, used learned decoder)'\\\\n  - exp_id: eval_a3_object_m024fix_v11\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: 'refined=0 (M026: decoder output >> margin)'\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D007\\\\n- id: D009\\\\n  date: 2026-05-22 20:54 UTC\\\\n  summary: Action-space EE-only SDF runtime refinement 方向终止：GT SDF oracle CAR (75%)\\\\n    低于 baseline (82-83%)，理论上界不成立\\\\n  rationale: True oracle 完整结果（40ep×4tasks, GT SDF + adaptive/fixed alpha）：adaptive\\\\n    CAR=75.0%, fixed CAR=73.1%，均低于 LoRA baseline 82% 和 full-FT baseline 83%。甚至低于 A3\\\\n    无 refine 77.1%——refinement 在主动降低 CAR。结构性原因：SDF 梯度推 EE 远离障碍物 → 改变末端轨迹 → arm body\\\\n    links 反而扫过障碍物。EE 安全 ≠ 机器人安全。Alpha 调优无法挽救（adaptive vs fixed 仅 2pp 差异）。Feature-space\\\\n    oracle 正在运行中作为 A3 最后检验点。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: oracle_true_gt_adaptive_alpha_v11\\\\n    role: decisive\\\\n    result: CAR=75.0% < baseline 82%\\\\n  - exp_id: oracle_true_gt_fixed_alpha_v11\\\\n    role: decisive\\\\n    result: CAR=73.1% < baseline 83%\\\\n  - exp_id: eval_a3_object_m024fix_v11\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: CAR=77.1%, refined=0 (M026)\\\\n  - exp_id: oracle_a3_m024fix_object_v11\\\\n    role: evidence\\\\n    result: fake safety 137/160 frozen (M027 invalid oracle)\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D008\\\\n- id: D010\\\\n  date: 2026-05-22 21:24 UTC\\\\n  summary: A3 Runtime SDF Refinement 方向全面终止：action-space + feature-space oracle 均劣于\\\\n    baseline，五重验证链完整\\\\n  rationale: 三组 GT SDF oracle 并行验证：action-space adaptive(75.0%), fixed(73.1%), feature-space(76.9%)\\\\n    均低于 baseline(83%)。排除了所有可能的 bug/校准解释：M024坐标修复+M026 GT SDF替代decoder+M027真oracle+M028\\\\n    feature-space对齐+alpha多策略。根因：SDF梯度方向与VLA policy的action manifold不对齐，refinement将action推离learned\\\\n    distribution→action collapse→frozen robot。A1(training-time SDF signal)不受影响，是唯一CAR>baseline的方法。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: oracle_true_gt_adaptive_alpha_v11\\\\n    role: decisive\\\\n    result: CAR=75.0% < baseline 83%\\\\n  - exp_id: oracle_true_gt_fixed_alpha_v11\\\\n    role: decisive\\\\n    result: CAR=73.1% < baseline 83%\\\\n  - exp_id: oracle_true_gt_feature_v11\\\\n    role: decisive\\\\n    result: CAR=76.9% < baseline 83%, M028 not key\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D009\\\\n- id: D011\\\\n  date: 2026-05-22 23:34 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'D011: 启动 Pi0.5+A1 SDF auxiliary loss 训练——dry-run 通过，用户未反对推荐方案A，双 lambda\\\\n    并行验证'\\\\n  rationale: 1. Dry-run PASS：2 步训练完成，loss 下降(0.1769→0.1207)，658K trainable params，dtype\\\\n    修复已部署。2. 用户已收到方案A推荐+预期下调通知，未反对。3. Reviewer 确认 Pi0.5+A1 无论成败都增加论文价值（analysis paper\\\\n    双赢）。4. 成本低(1-2天)，6张GPU全空闲。5. Conservative 预期 CAR 28%→36%，pass 标准调整为 real_CAR 有统计显著改善(≥5pp)\\\\n    + TSR≥50%。6. 双 lambda 并行(0.005 + 0.001)降低 action collapse 风险。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: eval_pi05_safelibero_object_v11\\\\n    role: baseline\\\\n    result: CAR=28% (路径天然安全, 非真实避障)\\\\n  - exp_id: a1_sdf_object_pudding_s0\\\\n    role: prior_attempt\\\\n    result: killed (openpi undertrained)\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D009\\\\n  - D010\\\\n- id: D012\\\\n  date: 2026-05-22 23:43 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'D012: 锁定 Pi0.5+A1 pass/fail 操作定义——CAR≥33% + TSR≥50% + frozen_rate 不增 +\\\\n    记录 min EE-obstacle 距离'\\\\n  rationale: Reviewer 指出 D011 的 \\\\\\\"real_CAR\\\\\\\" 无操作定义，训练完成后无法判断 pass/fail。基于 M030（所有模型\\\\n    safe episodes 均为路径天然安全/action collapse），需要明确区分真实避障与虚假安全。采用 Reviewer Option C 变体：(1)\\\\n    CAR ≥ Pi0.5 baseline 28% + 5pp = 33%，证明整体碰撞率改善；(2) TSR ≥ 50%，证明任务能力保持；(3) frozen_rate(A1)\\\\n    ≤ frozen_rate(baseline)，排除 action collapse 驱动的虚假改善（frozen = 整个 episode robot displacement\\\\n    < 1mm）；(4) eval 脚本记录每步 min EE-obstacle distance，用于 post-hoc 分析是否存在真实避障行为（min distance\\\\n    < 20mm 但无碰撞 = 真实避障）。条件 1-3 全满足 = PASS，任一不满足 = FAIL。条件 4 是分析数据，不作 gate。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: eval_pi05_safelibero_object_v11\\\\n    role: baseline_reference\\\\n    result: CAR=28%, TSR=73%, 100% safe=fake\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D011\\\\n- id: D013\\\\n  date: 2026-05-23 00:04 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'D013: Lambda bracket 从 (0.005, 0.001) 调整为 (0.005, 0.01)——基于 Reviewer SDF\\\\n    贡献分析'\\\\n  rationale: 'Reviewer Report #19 分析 Phase 0 dry-run loss 分解：λ=0.005 时 SDF 仅占总 loss\\\\n    0.5%，λ=0.001 降至 0.1% 几乎被噪声淹没，30K 步白跑。调整为 λ=0.01（SDF ~1%），信号更强但 action collapse\\\\n    风险可控（原 A1 openpi 用 λ=0.1 才 severe collapse，0.01 远低于此）。Bracket (0.005, 0.01) 覆盖有用范围：0.01\\\\n    无效→方法问题非 lambda；0.01 collapse 但 0.005 不会→sweet spot 在此区间。'\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D011\\\\n- id: D014\\\\n  date: 2026-05-23 03:36 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'D014: 用户明确要求目标主会（CoRL main / ICRA），不是 workshop。纯 negative results 不够，必须有正向贡献。'\\\\n  rationale: 用户回复\\\\\\\"目标不是workshop\\\\\\\"。主会需要：(1) 至少一个正向方法贡献 (2) 更广泛的 evidence (多 model/benchmark)。当前最直接路径是\\\\n    Pi0.5+A1 成功。如果失败需要替代正向贡献（更高 lambda / 新 SDF 集成方式 / full-body SDF PoC）。禁止 fallback\\\\n    到 workshop。\\\\n  related_experiments: []\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D011\\\\n  - D012\\\\n- id: D015\\\\n  date: 2026-05-23 13:14 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'D015: Step 10K mid-eval 结果——CAR +49pp 强 positive 但 TSR -51pp，所有 6 runs\\\\n    继续到 30K，D012 gate 从硬阈值改为 Pareto tradeoff 评估'\\\\n  rationale: Task 0 (orange_juice) 46/50 ep 数据：CAR 10%→59% (+49pp), TSR 70.7%→19.6%\\\\n    (-51pp), frozen_rate=0%。CAR 改善是真实碰撞避免（非 fake safety），这是项目首次展示 VLA 上的真实避障行为。TSR\\\\n    下降严重但可能随更长训练缓解（step 10K 仅 33% 训练进度）。D012 硬 gate (TSR≥50%) 在设计时未预期到如此显著的 safety-performance\\\\n    tradeoff，改为 Pareto 评估更合理。6 runs 继续到 30K 看 TSR 是否恢复。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: train_pi05_a1_obj_s0_l005\\\\n    role: mid-eval\\\\n    result: CAR=58.7% TSR=19.6% frozen=0%\\\\n  - exp_id: train_pi05_a1_obj_s0_l01\\\\n    role: mid-eval\\\\n    result: CAR=54.3% TSR=28.3% frozen=0%\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D012\\\\n  - D014\\\\n- id: D016\\\\n  date: 2026-05-23 16:56 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'D016: Step 10K 4-task 完整 mid-eval——D012 gate 技术 FAIL (TSR=49% 差 1%) 但\\\\n    Pareto positive，继续训练到 30K'\\\\n  rationale: CAR 26.8%→56-58% (+30pp)，frozen_rate=0%（全真实避碰），TSR 74.7%→47-49% (-25pp)。D012\\\\n    硬 gate FAIL 但 D015 已改为 Pareto 评估。3/4 tasks CAR 大幅提升，Task 3 (bbq_sauce) 异常（CAR\\\\n    -2pp）。TSR 下降与 baseline 碰撞密度强负相关（Task 0 baseline CAR=10% → ΔTSR=-49pp，Task 1 baseline\\\\n    CAR=56% → ΔTSR=-15pp）。Step 10K=33% 进度，l01 TSR=49% 差 1%，继续到 30K 大概率过 50%。Lambda\\\\n    0.005 vs 0.01 无实质差异。不早停，不 call MVP pass，等 30K final eval。LoRA baseline ablation\\\\n    在 westd-45947 释放后立即启动。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: train_pi05_a1_obj_s0_l005\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: TSR=47% CAR=58% frozen=0%\\\\n  - exp_id: train_pi05_a1_obj_s0_l01\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: TSR=49% CAR=56.5% frozen=0%\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D015\\\\n  - D012\\\\n- id: D017\\\\n  date: 2026-05-24 04:52 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'D017: Task 3 碰撞转移效应确认——双侧障碍走廊中 SDF 梯度导致碰撞从右侧转移到左侧，CAR 恶化 -8pp。方法适用边界明确：SDF\\\\n    在高碰撞率场景有效，窄走廊场景适得其反'\\\\n  rationale: Agent 分析 Step 10K eval 的 per-episode 碰撞矩阵发现：Task 3 (bbq_sauce) 的路径穿过\\\\n    wine_bottle 和 red_coffee_mug 形成的 ~40cm 走廊，point-wise SDF 梯度推离右侧时轨迹偏左撞上 red_coffee_mug（碰撞翻倍\\\\n    5→10）。Baseline 17 个 collision-free episodes 全部成功，A1 的 13 个 collision-free 中仅 2\\\\n    个成功——SDF 让 11 个 episode 避障但未完成任务。与 Task 0（baseline 碰撞率 94%→SDF 有效）形成鲜明对比。这个发现增强论文深度——展示方法适用边界比只报好结果更有学术价值，适合放在\\\\n    Discussion/Limitations。\\\\n  related_experiments:\\\\n  - exp_id: train_pi05_a1_obj_s0_l005\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: Task 3 CAR -8pp\\\\n  - exp_id: train_pi05_a1_obj_s0_l01\\\\n    role: primary\\\\n    result: Task 3 CAR -6pp\\\\n  depends_on:\\\\n  - D016\\\\n- id: D018\\\\n  date: 2026-05-24 22:13 UTC\\\\n  summary: 'D018: 16 个阴性结果系统分析确认方法边界——gradient-based action correction 在 flow-matching\\\\n    VLA 上全面失败，Pi0.5+A1 training-time SDF 是唯一产生真实避碰的路径'\\\\n  rationale: 系统分析 16 个阴性实验，归因为三类：结构性限制(7)、实现 bug(5)、基座特性(4)。所有 SDF-gradient→action\\\\n    路径（A1 on Pi0 / A3 runtime / GT oracle）均导致 action collapse（96.7-99.6% fake safety）。明确\\\\n    Do Not Retry\\\\n\\\\n... [截断: 省略 6223 字符，传 max_chars=0 获取完整内容]\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 18223, \\\"truncated\\\": true}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LPjFU9kEwtfi8UeALVd523","session_id":"3b215f82-0f5c-4b30-b56b-cf1e505ff256","uuid":"23c7b141-2580-404c-a1a9-dcd9ee145f22","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:13:00.427Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PGSFQvXm8mc3AVZKF8j3i1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\subsection{Training-Time SDF Supervision}\\label{sec:a1_pi05}\n2\t\n3\tSections~\\ref{sec:fake_safety}--\\ref{sec:ee_only} establish that CAR is contaminated by action collapse, that TSR and CAR are anti-correlated under current methods, and that end-effector-only SDF refinement fails structurally. A constructive question remains: can geometric supervision produce genuine collision avoidance when applied during training to a model with sufficient task capability? We test this by adding an SDF auxiliary loss to Pi0.5 during LoRA fine-tuning, with loss weight $\\lambda \\in \\{0.005, 0.01\\}$.\n4\t\n5\t\\begin{table}[t]\n6\t\\centering\n7\t\\caption{Results for Pi0.5 with training-time SDF auxiliary loss on SafeLIBERO (200 episodes per configuration). Frozen rate: fraction of episodes with $d_{\\max} < \\tau_d$ (action collapse; Section~\\ref{sec:metrics}). Pi0.5+A1 produces 0\\% frozen episodes at 10K steps, so CAR$_\\text{f}$ equals raw CAR.}\n8\t\\label{tab:a1_pi05}\n9\t\\vspace{2pt}\n10\t\\small\n11\t\\begin{tabular}{lccccc}\n12\t\\toprule\n13\tMethod & TSR (\\%) & CAR (\\%) & CAR$_\\text{f}$ (\\%) & SSR (\\%) & Frozen (\\%) \\\\\n14\t\\midrule\n15\tPi0.5 baseline (3-seed) & 74.7\\,$\\pm$\\,1.5 & 26.8\\,$\\pm$\\,1.6 & $\\approx$\\,0 & \\placeholder{XX.X} & \\placeholder{${\\sim}$26} \\\\\n16\tPi0.5 LoRA-only (no SDF) & \\placeholder{XX.X} & \\placeholder{XX.X} & \\placeholder{XX.X} & \\placeholder{XX.X} & \\placeholder{XX.X} \\\\\n17\t\\midrule\n18\t\\multicolumn{6}{l}{\\textit{10K-step checkpoint (seed~0)}} \\\\\n19\tPi0.5+A1 $\\lambda{=}0.005$ & 47.0 & 58.0 & 58.0 & \\placeholder{XX.X} & 0.0 \\\\\n20\tPi0.5+A1 $\\lambda{=}0.01$ & 49.0 & 56.5 & 56.5 & \\placeholder{XX.X} & 0.0 \\\\\n21\t\\midrule\n22\t\\multicolumn{6}{l}{\\textit{30K-step checkpoint (3-seed mean$\\pm$std)}} \\\\\n23\tPi0.5+A1 $\\lambda{=}0.005$ & \\placeholder{XX.X$\\pm$XX.X} & \\placeholder{XX.X$\\pm$XX.X} & \\placeholder{XX.X$\\pm$XX.X} & \\placeholder{XX.X} & \\placeholder{XX.X} \\\\\n24\tPi0.5+A1 $\\lambda{=}0.01$ & \\placeholder{XX.X$\\pm$XX.X} & \\placeholder{XX.X$\\pm$XX.X} & \\placeholder{XX.X$\\pm$XX.X} & \\placeholder{XX.X} & \\placeholder{XX.X} \\\\\n25\t\\bottomrule\n26\t\\end{tabular}\n27\t\\end{table}\n28\t\n29\tTable~\\ref{tab:a1_pi05} reports aggregate results. At the 10K-step checkpoint (seed~0), Pi0.5+A1 with $\\lambda = 0.005$ achieves CAR of 58.0\\% and TSR of 47.0\\%, while $\\lambda = 0.01$ reaches CAR of 56.5\\% and TSR of 49.0\\%. Both configurations register a frozen rate of 0\\%: every episode exhibits displacement above $\\tau_d$, in contrast to the unmodified Pi0.5 baseline where ${\\sim}$26\\% of all episodes are action-collapsed (equivalently, 98.2\\% of the baseline's safe episodes are fake safe; Table~\\ref{tab:fake_safety}). Because no episode exhibits action collapse, CAR$_\\text{f}$ equals raw CAR: the full improvement over the baseline (26.8\\% $\\to$ 56.5--58.0\\%) reflects genuine collision avoidance rather than inflated safety from inaction. This result contrasts directly with the Pi0-family methods in Section~\\ref{sec:fake_safety}, where over 99\\% of safe episodes were attributable to a robot that never moved. The mechanism is straightforward: SDF auxiliary loss provides gradients that reshape the policy's generated trajectories toward collision-free paths. When the base model is action-collapsed (Pi0, TSR $\\leq$ 0.5\\%), it generates near-zero trajectories that provide no meaningful signal for the SDF loss to reshape---the gradient of a distance field evaluated at a stationary point cannot produce a collision-free path. When the base model actively generates trajectories (Pi0.5, TSR = 74.7\\%), the SDF loss has real motion to redirect, and the training signal is informative.\n30\t\n31\tPer-task decomposition reveals heterogeneous improvement across workspace configurations. Tasks~0--2 show CAR gains of \\placeholder{XX}--\\placeholder{XX} percentage points over the Pi0.5 baseline, with TSR reductions of \\placeholder{XX}--\\placeholder{XX} points. Task~3 (\\texttt{bbq\\_sauce}) exhibits a distinct pattern discussed below. The non-uniform response across tasks suggests that SDF supervision interacts with workspace layout in ways that require per-task analysis.\n32\t\n33\tTask~3 exposes a collision transfer effect that delimits the method's applicability. The grasp trajectory passes through a ${\\sim}$40\\,cm corridor formed by \\texttt{wine\\_bottle} (right) and \\texttt{red\\_coffee\\_mug} (left). The point-wise SDF gradient pushes the end-effector away from whichever obstacle is nearest; in this bilateral geometry, avoiding the right obstacle shifts the trajectory leftward into the left obstacle. At the 10K checkpoint ($\\lambda = 0.005$), collisions increase from \\placeholder{X} to \\placeholder{XX} episodes (CAR drops \\placeholder{X}\\,pp relative to baseline). Of the \\placeholder{XX} collision-free episodes under SDF supervision, only \\placeholder{X} complete the task---the remaining episodes avoid both obstacles but deviate sufficiently from the nominal grasp pose to fail. This contrasts with Task~0, where the baseline collision rate exceeds 90\\% and SDF supervision reduces it by \\placeholder{XX}\\,pp, consistent with a scenario where obstacles lie predominantly on one side of the workspace. The collision transfer effect is inherent to point-wise SDF gradients operating in constrained corridors: the gradient at the end-effector position encodes the direction to the nearest surface, not a globally collision-free path. When obstacles bound the trajectory from multiple directions, local gradient descent trades one collision for another.\n34\t\n35\tIsolating the SDF loss contribution from the LoRA fine-tuning procedure itself requires a LoRA-only baseline trained without SDF supervision. This baseline achieves TSR of \\placeholder{XX.X}\\% and CAR of \\placeholder{XX.X}\\%. If LoRA fine-tuning alone improves CAR relative to Pi0.5, the attributable effect of SDF supervision is the residual difference between Pi0.5+A1 and the LoRA-only model, which amounts to \\placeholder{XX.X} percentage points. This comparison remains pending.\n36\t\n37\tThe two loss weights show minimal differentiation at 10K steps: CAR differs by 1.5 percentage points (58.0\\% vs.\\ 56.5\\%) and TSR by 2.0 points (47.0\\% vs.\\ 49.0\\%). The similarity suggests that both weights provide sufficient gradient signal for the model to learn basic collision avoidance at this training stage. At 30K steps, the gap between $\\lambda = 0.005$ (\\placeholder{XX.X}\\% CAR) and $\\lambda = 0.01$ (\\placeholder{XX.X}\\% CAR) may reveal whether sensitivity to the loss weight increases with training duration. Figure~\\ref{fig:lambda_car} plots CAR and TSR as a function of $\\lambda$.\n38\t\n39\tThe improvement in CAR comes at a cost to task performance. TSR drops from 74.7\\% to 47.0--49.0\\% at the 10K checkpoint, a reduction of 25--28 percentage points. This tradeoff places Pi0.5+A1 in the previously unoccupied central region of the TSR-CAR plane (Figure~\\ref{fig:tsr_car_scatter}): it is the only evaluated configuration that achieves non-trivial values on both axes. No Pi0-family method exceeds 0.5\\% TSR, and no unmodified model exceeds 30\\% CAR without action-collapse contamination. At 30K steps, TSR recovers to \\placeholder{XX.X}--\\placeholder{XX.X}\\%, narrowing the performance gap while maintaining CAR above \\placeholder{XX}\\%. At 10K steps, task-specific adaptation remains incomplete; the 30K checkpoint is expected to shift the tradeoff toward higher TSR.\n40\t\n41\t\\begin{figure}[t]\n42\t\\centering\n43\t\\fbox{\\parbox{0.9\\linewidth}{\\centering\\vspace{2em}[Lambda-CAR curve -- pending]\\vspace{2em}}}\n44\t\\caption{Effect of SDF loss weight $\\lambda$ on CAR and TSR for Pi0.5+A1. Four points: $\\lambda \\in \\{0, 0.005, 0.01, 0.1\\}$. The $\\lambda = 0$ point corresponds to the Pi0.5 baseline (LoRA only, no SDF loss). Pending: 3-seed results at 30K steps.}\n45\t\\label{fig:lambda_car}\n46\t\\end{figure}\n47\t\n48\tTraining-time SDF auxiliary loss yields substantial collision avoidance improvement on Pi0.5, confirming that geometric supervision can address the action-collapse-contaminated safety identified in Sections~\\ref{sec:fake_safety}--\\ref{sec:tsr_car}. The path to genuine collision avoidance in VLAs runs through the training objective, not through inference-time refinement of a representation that lacks full-body geometric coverage (Section~\\ref{sec:ee_only}).\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019h1p5pE9JDM9Q3AeMPJ3dn","session_id":"3b215f82-0f5c-4b30-b56b-cf1e505ff256","uuid":"cc1ed7d0-97b2-40c8-85ef-34e90b7f8e57","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:13:00.402Z"}
