{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BURjA9gcQPWE1Vy9ip9WXs","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/paper/main.bbl:73:\\newblock {OpenVLA}: An open-source vision-language-action model.\ndocs/paper/discussion.tex:6:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/discussion.tex:9:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/introduction.tex:5:[Omitted long matching line]\ndocs/paper/references.bib:15:  title={{OpenVLA}: An Open-Source Vision-Language-Action Model},\ndocs/paper/_archive/conclusion_DEPRECATED.tex:5:\\paragraph{Limitations.} Our evaluation is limited to two SafeLIBERO scenes in simulation; broader task coverage and real-robot transfer remain to be demonstrated. The SDF ground truth requires known obstacle meshes, which are available in simulation but would require reconstruction methods (e.g., neural SDF from depth observations) for real-world deployment. The method is validated on a single base VLA ($\\pi_0$); generalization to other architectures (OpenVLA, RT-2) is an open question."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LPjFU9kEwtfi8UeALVd523","session_id":"3b215f82-0f5c-4b30-b56b-cf1e505ff256","uuid":"a4e51419-d3a4-4b77-9216-590abddd1851","timestamp":"2026-05-25T23:13:08.234Z"}
